<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Director, are you able to tell us why we are digging up something so dangerous?\'94 Agent Kimberley asked innocently.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I have not been able to tell you until now, until all your security checks and transfer orders had been completed. Now I can unequivocally say, ladies and gentlemen, you are the elite of the agency and have been selected for this task due to your commitment to freedom and democracy.\'94 
\f2\i Also because you are all so eminently disposable, he thought.
\f1\i0  \'93The Primary Trade Dominion faces the greatest peril since its formation 50 years ago. There is a cancer, creeping silently through our souls, eating away at our very way of life. This cancer is the Elvi.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Surely not, Director. They are just entertainers, aren\'92t they?\'94 Agent Kimberly again showed his naivety. Director Hardman decided this guy would be the first to go.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93That is precisely what they want us all to think. That they are merely a loveable bunch of singers, dancers and bartenders, whose sole purpose for being is to entertain us, but they are nothing of the sort. They organise and conspire against the PTD. Their concerts are filled with subversive political commentary aimed at undermining the natural order and to ultimately change the structure of our society, placing themselves at the top. The lyrics to many songs are direct threats to vital industries that thrive under our deregulated system. Coal producers are livid and they are threatening mass sackings if something is not done. It\'92s the same with the power companies.\'94
